          "  // Auto-save when generation completes\n  const messageCount = chatHistory.messages?.length;\n  const lastMessageId = lastMessageInHistory?.id;\n  const isLastMessageGenerating = lastMessageInHistory?.isGenerating;\n  // saveCurrentChat also changes on edits that shouldn't save (e.g. the\n  // current prompt), so only save when the messages state itself changes\n  const lastAutoSaveTriggerRef = useRef<{\n    isLastMessageGenerating: boolean | undefined;\n    lastMessageId: string | undefined;\n    messageCount: number | undefined;\n  } | null>(null);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const lastTrigger = lastAutoSaveTriggerRef.current;\n    if (\n      lastTrigger &&\n      lastTrigger.messageCount === messageCount &&\n      lastTrigger.lastMessageId === lastMessageId &&\n      lastTrigger.isLastMessageGenerating"
        ],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed all four issues by editing the two effects in `useTTDChatStorage.ts`. I couldn't re-run the linter or the type checker: there's no `node_modules`, and downloading oxlint needed approval this non-interactive run can't give. So the fixes are reasoned through against both rules, not confirmed by a lint run.\n\n**Issues 1 and 3 (initial load effect, line 185):** I added `loadChats` to the dependency array. The effect can now re-run whenever `loadChats` changes, but `loadChats` returns early once chats are loading or loaded, so in practice it still loads once. The one difference: if other code resets the exported `chatsLoadedAtom` to `false`, the chats will now reload.\n\n**Issues 2 and 4 (auto-save effect, line 252):** I didn't just list `saveCurrentChat` as a dependency, because that changes behaviour. It changes whenever anything in `chatHistory` changes, such as typing in the prompt, so the hook would call `persistenceAdapter.saveChats` on every keystroke. It could also loop forever if a caller creates the adapter inline.\n\nInstead:\n- The three trigger values (message count, last message id, last message's `isGenerating`) are now local variables that the effect reads.\n- A ref, `lastAutoSaveTriggerRef`, records the values from the last save attempt. The effect only saves when one of them has actually changed and the last message isn't generating.\n- The dependency array is now exactly what the effect uses: `isLastMessageGenerating`, `lastMessageId`, `messageCount`, `saveCurrentChat`. This also clears the \"unnecessary dependency\" part of issue 2.\n\nSaves happen at the same moments as before. The only difference is in development under StrictMode: the original saved twice on mount, and this version saves once.",
